      "text": "## The Big Picture"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md#002",
      "path": [
        "01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:embedded-systems:01-microcontrollers, git-history:embedded-systems:01-microcontrollers]",
        "canonical_path": "embedded-systems/01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md",
        "concepts": "[microcontroller, cortex-m, memory map, mcu, mpu, soc]",
        "current_path": "embedded-systems/01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md",
        "id": "maxim:embedded-systems:microcontrollers",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "embedded-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[microcontroller]",
        "section": "embedded-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microcontrollers - MCU, MPU, SoC and the ARM Cortex-M",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A microcontroller is a complete computer on one die: CPU, program memory\n(flash), working memory (SRAM), and a pile of peripherals, wired by internal\nbuses. Unlike the server CPU you know — which is a core surrounded by *external*\nDRAM and a chipset — the MCU's defining feature is that it boots and runs\nentirely from on-chip resources. The map below is the territory you program."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:embedded-systems:01-microcontrollers, git-history:embedded-systems:01-microcontrollers]",
        "canonical_path": "embedded-systems/01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md",
        "concepts": "[microcontroller, cortex-m, memory map, mcu, mpu, soc]",
        "current_path": "embedded-systems/01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md",
        "id": "maxim:embedded-systems:microcontrollers",
        "index_roles": "[guide]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "embedded-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[microcontroller]",
        "section": "embedded-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microcontrollers - MCU, MPU, SoC and the ARM Cortex-M",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                      A TYPICAL Cortex-M MCU                           |\n|                                                                       |\n|  .----------------.        .-----------------------------------.      |\n|  |  CPU CORE      |        |  NVIC (interrupt controller)      |      |\n|  |  Cortex-M4F    |<------>|  prioritizes + vectors IRQs       |      |\n|  |  + FPU         |        '-----------------------------------'      |\n|  |  + SysTick     |                  ^                                |\n|  '-------'--------'                  | IRQ lines                      |\n|          |  AHB bus                  |                                |\n|  .-------.-------------------------------------------------.          |\n|  |                  BUS MATRIX (AHB/APB)                   |          |\n|  '--'--------'--------'--------'--------'--------'---------'          |\n|     |        |        |        |        |        |         |          |\n|     v        v        v        v        v        v         v          |\n|  .-----. .------. .------. .------. .------. .-----. .---------.      |\n|  |FLASH| | SRAM | | GPIO | | UART | | SPI  | | ADC | |  DMA    |      |\n|  |512KB| |128KB | |ports | | I2C  | | CAN  | | DAC | |engine   |      |\n|  '-----' '------' '------' '------' '------' '-----' '---------'      |\n|                                                                       |\n|  +-----------------------------------------------------------+        |\n|  | CLOCK TREE (PLL, prescalers) | POWER (regulators, modes)  |        |\n|  +-----------------------------------------------------------+        |\n+-----------------------------------------------------------------------+\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md#004",
      "path": [
        "01-MICROCONTROLLERS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
