        "section": "embedded-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Microcontrollers - MCU, MPU, SoC and the ARM Cortex-M",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Read this as a small city.** The core is downtown; the bus matrix is the\nroad network; flash and SRAM are the warehouses; peripherals are the factories\non the edge of town. The NVIC is the dispatch center that interrupts the core\nwhen a factory needs attention. Most of the die area is *not* the core."
    },
